  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Konijnen. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Konijnen (Dutch for 'Rabbits') is a fast-paced, family-friendly shedding game popular in the Netherlands and Scandinavia (where it is known as 'Kanin'). The objective is to be the first to empty your hand by playing cards into numerical sequences on the table. It is known for its speed and the 'tactical shifting' rules that allow players to rearrange table piles to fit their cards.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to discard all your cards by placing them into numerical sequences on the table.',
    gameplay: "1. Players take turns clockwise.\n2. On your turn, you must play as many cards as possible into existing sequences or start new ones.\n3. **Starting Sequences**: A new sequence must start with an Ace (1) or a Two (2).\n4. **Building**: You can add a card to any sequence if it is exactly one rank higher than the current top card (e.g., a 7 on a 6).\n5. **Shifting (Tactical Maneuver)**: Some house rules allow you to 'break' a long sequence (e.g., 1-2-3-4-5) to start a new branch if you have the cards to support both (e.g., moving the 4-5 to a different pile).\n6. **Drawing**: If you cannot play at least one card, you must draw one from the stock and your turn ends.",
    keyRules: [
      'New sequences start with Ace or 2 only.',
      'Building: add a card exactly one rank higher than the current top of any sequence.',
      'If you cannot play at least one card, you must draw one from the stock and your turn ends.',
      'First player to empty their hand wins.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 5 players; 3 to 4 is optimal.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces are low (1).',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces are low (1).',
      dealing: 'Each player is dealt 7 to 10 cards. The remainder forms the draw pile.',
