    turnFlow: "1. Players take turns clockwise.\n2. On your turn, you must play as many cards as possible into existing sequences or start new ones.\n3. **Starting Sequences**: A new sequence must start with an Ace (1) or a Two (2).\n4. **Building**: You can add a card to any sequence if it is exactly one rank higher than the current top card (e.g., a 7 on a 6).\n5. **Shifting (Tactical Maneuver)**: Some house rules allow you to 'break' a long sequence (e.g., 1-2-3-4-5) to start a new branch if you have the cards to support both (e.g., moving the 4-5 to a different pile).\n6. **Drawing**: If you cannot play at least one card, you must draw one from the stock and your turn ends.",
